  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "UA_Server_new",
    "file": "open62541/plugins/ua_config_default.c",
    "description": "UA_Server_new creates a temporary UA_ServerConfig on the stack, initializes config.nodestore, then passes it to UA_Server_newWithConfig, which shallow-copies the config into server->config. On init failure, UA_Server_newWithConfig/UA_Server_delete calls UA_ServerConfig_clean and frees nodestore.context. UA_Server_new then incorrectly calls config.nodestore.clear(config.nodestore.context) again when server==NULL, causing a second free/use-after-free in UA_NodeMap_delete.",
    "conditions": "Triggered when UA_Server_newWithConfig fails during UA_Server_init (as in fuzz_binary_message with tiny/invalid input), so cleanup happens internally via UA_Server_delete -> UA_ServerConfig_clean first. Because UA_Server_new still owns the same stack config and does not know ownership was transferred/shallow-copied, its error path performs duplicate nodestore cleanup. The PoV reaches this with 0-length fuzz input path that causes early server init failure."
  },
